    "narrative": "Today\u2019s lineup is anchored by **Bryce Harper**, who earns our highest efficiency score of 72.35 against Sandy Alcantara. Beyond the elite talent, **Bryce Harper** benefits from a massive 8% BvP boost over 57 career plate appearances and an ideal #3 spot in the order, positioning him to capitalize on run-scoring opportunities. Similarly, **Geraldo Perdomo** presents as a primary value play at 68.75. Despite a moderate rain risk, he benefits from a favorable wind-out environment and a high-leverage #2 spot in the order facing Bubba Chandler. **Dylan Beavers** rounds out the top tier of the outfield at 63.23; he is a priority start today, as the combination of an leadoff role, positive wind factors, and a strong platoon split against Troy Melton outweighs the slight drag from the pitcher\u2019s base skill.\n\nThe most difficult decision on today\u2019s slate involved the final outfield and bench spots. **Daulton Varsho** nearly forced his way into the lineup with a score of 51.40; while his platoon edge against Cade Cavalli is significant, he was ultimately edged out by the superior power-environment projection of **Gavin Sheets** and the lineup flexibility provided by **Jonathan Aranda**. We are closely monitoring the 31% rain risk affecting **Geraldo Perdomo** and **Ryan Waldschmidt**, though both remain active starts as the atmospheric factors are currently tilted in favor of the hitter. Investors should note that while **Cal Raleigh** and **Yainer Diaz** are currently locked in, both are subject to late-afternoon adjustments if official lineups move them down in the batting order, which could compress their current efficiency scores.",
